cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HelioFleet in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "HelioFleet: an interactive map of heliophysics spacecraft positions"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dash
    given-names: Soumyaranjan
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0103-6569"
    affiliation: "National Solar Observatory"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-12
url: "https://sr-dash.github.io/heliofleet/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sr-dash/heliofleet"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  HelioFleet is a web tool that shows where heliophysics spacecraft (SDO,
  SOHO, Aditya-L1, ACE, Wind, DSCOVR, Solar Orbiter, Parker Solar Probe,
  BepiColombo, STEREO-A/B and MAVEN) are relative to the Sun and Earth on any
  date since 2010. It reports Stonyhurst and Carrington coordinates and
  Parker-spiral footpoints, searches for radial alignments, quadratures and
  magnetic connections, checks which observers see a given point on the Sun,
  and exports coordinates and time series. Positions come from JPL Horizons
  ephemerides, refreshed monthly.
keywords:
  - heliophysics
  - spacecraft ephemerides
  - solar physics
  - multi-spacecraft observations
  - solar eclipse
  - space weather
  - JPL Horizons
